Up Your Arsenal's online play (the multiplayer executable, I5BOOTN.ELF) goes to the OpenRAC server instead of the retail Medius, DME and DNAS servers. Only the multiplayer path changes.

**What it does** (`port/game/rac3-pal/host/mp_net.c`, the rows of `mp/libraries.tsv` naming it; README "Online play"):

- the network adaptor, its configuration and interface are there; the IOP-only start-up steps (module loads, MSIF RPC, the USB headset) are skipped;
- DNAS passes at once and the servers' names resolve;
- Medius is answered at the message level by a small lobby in the port, whose replies go through the library's own dispatcher: logging in says hello to the server, the game list is the server's party list with each host's advert, creating a game hosts a party, joining one joins it;
- DME runs at the session level: the game room is the party, its client indices the party's order, and every DME message is relayed to the other members (the server's new `RELAY`).
- hostgen gets the SCE-RT,

